</div>

<div class="bg-gray-50 py-20 px-4">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <section aria-labelledby="problem-heading">
      <div class="text-center">
        <h2 id="problem-heading" class="mb-4 text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">
          Sound familiar?
        </h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mb-12 max-w-2xl text-lg text-gray-600">
          Every WhatsApp seller deals with this every single day.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <article class="flex h-full flex-col rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
          <div class="mb-4 text-4xl" aria-hidden="true">😤</div>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Orders buried in WhatsApp chats</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
            You're copy-pasting buyer details, checking addresses manually, and creating Delhivery shipments one by one. Hours of work every day that should be automatic.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="flex h-full flex-col rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
          <div class="mb-4 text-4xl" aria-hidden="true">💸</div>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">₹150+ lost on every RTO</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
            Forward shipping ₹80. Return ₹70. Zero revenue. 20-40% of COD orders come back. That's thousands of rupees gone every month — for orders that were never real.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="flex h-full flex-col rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 bg-white p-8 shadow-sm">
          <div class="mb-4 text-4xl" aria-hidden="true">😰</div>
          <h3 class="mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Buyers keep asking where is my order</h3>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-600">
            You check Delhivery manually, find the tracking link, and paste it to every buyer individually. Every. Single. Time. While new orders keep coming in.
          </p>
